# Netlify Redirects Configuration
# Documentation: https://docs.netlify.com/routing/redirects/

# SPA (Single Page Application) Fallback
# All routes are directed to index.html to enable client-side routing
# This prevents 404 errors when accessing deep links directly
/* /index.html 200

# Blog URL Redirects - Permanent redirects for moved content
# These help maintain SEO when blog posts are relocated
#/blog/old-post-1 /blog/new-post-1 301
#/blog/old-post-2 /blog/new-post-2 301

# HTTPS Enforcement (commented out as Netlify often handles this automatically)
# Uncomment if you need explicit control over HTTPS redirection
# http://example.com/* https://example.com/:splat 301!
